// - **Tenant-id**: Source of truth = auth (JWT/mTLS). Without auth, can be empty.
// - **Namespace**: Source of truth = application (when deploying) or actor (when created).
//    If actor is part of an app, namespace must match app namespace (error if mismatch).
// - **RequestContext**: Carries tenant_id + namespace through the stack. Tenant from HTTP/gRPC
//    request (auth); namespace from application/actor or passed with request for services like
//    keyvalue/tuplespace.
//
// ## Enforcement Points
// All PlexSpaces components enforce isolation at these levels:
// 1. **ActorRegistry**: Actors only visible within same tenant_id + namespace
// 2. **Messaging**: Messages cannot cross tenant boundaries (unless explicit policy)
// 3. **TupleSpace**: Tuples isolated per tenant + namespace
// 4. **Journal**: Events stored with tenant_id for GDPR compliance
// 5. **Supervision**: Supervisors scoped to tenant + namespace
